---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { sourceUrl, site } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Architecture and philosophy" description="Terminal host → NMSh frontend → ShellAdapter → real persistent shell. Understand the runtime, ownership, privacy and open-source project.">
  <div class="container"><header class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Architecture / A clear division of responsibility</span><h1>A frontend.<br />Not a replacement.</h1><p class="lead">NMSh improves the interaction around your commands. The shell still interprets them, and your terminal still owns the window.</p></header>
    <ol class="flow-diagram" aria-label="Runtime layers"><li><strong>Terminal host</strong><span>Window, fonts, cells, protocols</span></li><li><strong>NMSh frontend</strong><span>Composer, transcript, context</span></li><li><strong>ShellAdapter + PTY</strong><span>Bootstrap, transport, lifecycle</span></li><li><strong>Real shell</strong><span>zsh · Bash 4.4+ · Fish</span></li></ol>
    <section class="section split"><div class="split-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Continuity, not reconstruction</span><h2>One shell.<br />Between commands, too.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>A ShellSession owns a pseudo-terminal running a real persistent shell. Normally a separate local session service owns that PTY; the frontend attaches as a client. An in-process fallback exists.</p><p>Working directory, aliases, functions, environment and jobs persist because the shell persists. Closing a frontend window is different from terminating the service or shell. A saved transcript is a record, not a running process.</p><p>For fullscreen and interactive applications, NMSh suspends its presentation and uses passthrough. The program's real terminal interaction remains authoritative.</p><a href="/docs/reference/architecture/">Read the runtime architecture →</a></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>What belongs where.</h2><p>Keeping boundaries explicit makes compatibility easier to reason about—and prevents the frontend from quietly becoming something else.</p></div><div class="feature-row"><h3>The terminal host</h3><p>Owns its window, font rendering, terminal protocols, keyboard forwarding and standard text selection.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/shells/">Host compatibility <span>→</span></a></div><div class="feature-row"><h3>NMSh</h3><p>Owns the composer, completion menu, transcript presentation, panels, native context and frontend preferences.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/core-concepts/">Core concepts <span>→</span></a></div><div class="feature-row"><h3>Your shell</h3><p>Owns parsing, expansion, aliases, functions, command execution, environment and shell jobs.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/reference/shell-adapter/">ShellAdapter <span>→</span></a></div></section>
    <section class="section split"><div class="split-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Local-first, with explicit authority</span><h2>Your configuration<br />stays yours.</h2><p>No account, cloud typing service or telemetry. Local session records can still hold sensitive command output, so review what you export or share.</p></div><div><ol class="number-list"><li><div><strong>Configuration is executable.</strong><p>Shell rc files and framework code are not silently sourced, merged or edited by an import workflow. Offered edits are exact diffs behind confirmation.</p></div></li><li><div><strong>Discovery is not execution.</strong><p>Context inspection uses bounded local data. Opening a repository must not run its scripts or credential helpers.</p></div></li><li><div><strong>Ownership is evidence.</strong><p>Managed files are removed or replaced only while NMSh can prove they still match what it wrote.</p></div></li></ol><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/docs/reference/security/">Security <span>→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/docs/reference/privacy/">Privacy <span>→</span></a></div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="callout-band"><div><h2>Independent. Open source.</h2><p>notMyShell is made by raiseCatError and licensed GPL-3.0-only. No fictional company, commercial tiers or adoption claims. Just a public project, with its decisions and limitations in the open.</p></div><a class="button secondary" href={site.repo}>View the source <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/docs/reference/contributing/">Contribute <span>→</span></a><a class="text-link" href={sourceUrl('SUPPORT.md')}>Get support <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={`${site.repo}/issues/new?template=bug_report.yml`}>Report a bug <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
  </div>
</Base>
